# .trivyignore for the idp-portal (Backstage) container image.
#
# ─── POLICY ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Same convention as platform-hello/.trivyignore (Phase 7 bug #3):
#   - Only CVEs we deliberately tolerate get listed here
#   - Every entry needs a REASON + a REVIEW DATE
#   - Trivy still prints these on every CI run (gitleaks-style visibility)
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# ─── CONTEXT (why so many at once) ──────────────────────────────────
# Backstage's own package.json pulls in ~1700 transitive deps. 26 of
# them have published CVEs as of 2026-10-27 — all HIGH or CRITICAL,
# almost all Denial-of-Service in widely-used libraries (brace-expansion,
# tar, undici, picomatch, basic-ftp, @graphql-tools/utils, ...).
#
# For OUR deployment context:
#   1. Backstage runs behind an Ingress with TLS + authenticated session
#      (guest mode on kind; GitHub OAuth or SSO on EKS per Phase 9)
#   2. Request rate-limiting is applied at the Ingress / LB layer
#   3. The DoS CVEs are exploitable by sending crafted inputs; our
#      threat model has those inputs already filtered by the auth
#      proxy before they reach Backstage's Node runtime
#   4. The one Backstage-SPECIFIC CVE (CVE-2026-106492, service
#      credential delegation bypass in @backstage/backend-defaults
#      <0.17.8) requires a direct Backstage dep bump — out of scope
#      for a kind-local MVP; Phase 8 security hardening addresses it
#      together with the whole CVE sweep
#
# Full remediation (bump @backstage/* + yarn resolutions for transitives
# that have risky major-version jumps like tar 6→7, undici 5→6,
# @graphql-tools/utils 8→12) is a dedicated Phase 8 sub-wave.
#
# Review cycle: WEEKLY (7-day). The upstream Backstage team ships a
# release every 2 weeks and the latest release almost always resolves
# a chunk of these transitives. Re-fetch scan output; remove entries
# whose latest-tag Backstage has fixed; keep + document the rest.
# Next review: 2026-11-03
#
# ─── CVEs: @backstage/backend-defaults ──────────────────────────────
# Access control bypass via improper service credential delegation.
# Fix: @backstage/backend-defaults >= 0.17.8 (we're on 0.12.3).
# Mitigation: Backstage runs with auth=guest on kind; no credential
# delegation surface exploitable without first bypassing the ingress.
CVE-2026-106492

# ─── CVEs: @fastify/busboy ──────────────────────────────────────────
# DoS from crafted form-data headers. Fix: 3.2.1 (we're on 2.1.1).
# Mitigation: Backstage's form endpoints are all authenticated.
CVE-2026-19481

# ─── CVEs: @graphql-tools/utils ─────────────────────────────────────
# DoS via prototype pollution in mergeDeep. Fix: 12.0.1 (we're on 8.x).
# Mitigation: Backstage doesn't expose GraphQL mutations to anonymous
# traffic; prototype pollution requires attacker-controlled input to
# mergeDeep which is only reached via internal API calls.
CVE-2026-104852

# ─── CVEs: basic-ftp ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DoS via crafted Unix directory listings. Fix: 6.2.1 (we're on 5.3.1).
# Mitigation: Backstage doesn't initiate FTP from user input.
CVE-2026-102990

# ─── CVEs: brace-expansion ──────────────────────────────────────────
# 5 DoS variants (stack exhaustion, uncontrolled recursion, exponential
# complexity, memory exhaustion, unbounded intermediate arrays).
# Fix: 2.1.5+ (we're on 2.0.2). Mitigation: brace-expansion is used
# internally by glob matching; no user-controlled brace patterns reach it.
CVE-2026-102276
CVE-2026-102278
CVE-2026-13149
CVE-2026-14257
CVE-2026-69152

# ─── CVEs: ip-address ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# SSRF via inconsistent IP address parsing. Fix: 10.3.1 (we're on 10.1.0).
# Mitigation: Backstage's UrlReader has deny-by-default SSRF protection
# (ADR applied in Phase 5 Wave 1 for raw.githubusercontent.com allow).
CVE-2026-69192

# ─── CVEs: pacote ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DoS via crafted spec.rawSpec in addGitSha. Fix: 21.5.1 (we're on 19/20).
# Mitigation: pacote is used by @backstage/cli for scaffolder templates;
# no user-controlled npm specs reach it in our deployment (templates
# are curated, not user-authored).
CVE-2026-9496

# ─── CVEs: picomatch ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ReDoS via crafted extglob patterns. Fix: 4.0.4 (we're on 4.0.3).
# Mitigation: picomatch is used in glob matching internally; no
# user-controlled glob patterns reach it.
CVE-2026-33671

# ─── CVEs: sigstore ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Unauthorized certificates accepted. Fix: 4.1.1 (we're on 3.1.0).
# Mitigation: Backstage doesn't do image signature verification itself
# (that's Phase 8 Kyverno's job).
CVE-2026-48815

# ─── CVEs: tar (node-tar) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# 8 CVEs: gzip bomb DoS (CRITICAL), arbitrary file overwrite via
# path/symlink attacks, hardlink traversal, long-path DoS, malformed
# archive DoS. Fix: 7.5.19+ (we're on 6.2.1).
# Mitigation: tar is used by yarn install itself + by scaffolder
# template fetching. Yarn install only runs at build time (not
# runtime), and scaffolder templates come from a curated repo.
CVE-2026-23745
CVE-2026-23950
CVE-2026-24842
CVE-2026-26960
CVE-2026-29786
CVE-2026-31802
CVE-2026-59873
CVE-2026-59874
CVE-2026-73566

# ─── CVEs: undici ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 3 DoS CVEs (unbounded memory, invalid WebSocket). Fix: 6.27.0+ (we're
# on 5.29.0). Mitigation: undici is Backstage's HTTP client for internal
# service-to-service calls (K8s API, GitHub API). Not exposed to
# untrusted inputs.
CVE-2026-12151
CVE-2026-1526
CVE-2026-2229

# ─── CVEs: urllib ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Credential leakage via cross-origin redirects. Fix: 4.9.1 (we're on
# 3.27.3). Mitigation: Backstage doesn't follow user-controlled redirects.
CVE-2026-55553

# ─── NEW (added after Trivy DB refresh 2026-10-27) ──────────────────
# ─── CVEs: @azure/msal-node ─────────────────────────────────────────
# MSAL Node authorization code flow may disclose parameters to third
# parties. Fix: 7.1.0 (we're on 6.0.1). Mitigation: msal-node is
# transitively pulled by @backstage/plugin-auth-backend-module-azure
# which we don't configure/use — Azure OAuth is not enabled in our
# auth providers list.
CVE-2026-109461

# ─── CVEs: body-parser ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# DoS via unhandled exception on malformed JSON. Fix: 1.20.9 (we're
# on 1.20.8 — one patch bump away). Mitigation: express/body-parser
# is behind the auth proxy; malformed JSON would 400 quickly.
CVE-2026-111181

# ─── CVEs: markdown-it ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# DoS via unclosed autolink patterns. Fix: 14.3.3 (we're on 14.3.2).
# Mitigation: markdown-it is used by TechDocs rendering; techdocs is
# disabled in our MVP (no catalog pages trigger it).
CVE-2026-111758

# ─── CVEs: multer ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DoS via aborted request during multipart upload. Fix: 2.5.0 (we're
# on 2.4.0). Mitigation: no scaffolder uploads enabled in Wave 2
# (Wave 3 may; revisit then).
CVE-2026-113872

# ─── CVEs: undici (second finding) ──────────────────────────────────
# DoS via unhandled stream error. Fix: 7.30.1 (one found at 7.30.0,
# other transitive on 6.x). Shares the mitigation of the earlier
# undici entries — internal in-cluster HTTP client only.
CVE-2026-109869

# ─── CVEs: zod ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DoS via unbounded array validation. Fix: 4.6.6 (we're on 3.25.76 —
# 1 major jump risk). Mitigation: zod validates INTERNAL types in
# Backstage; no user-controlled schema input reaches it.
CVE-2023-54404

# ─── CVEs: undici (third finding, 2026-10-29) ───────────────────────
# 3 more undici CVEs surfaced when Wave 3 plugins (ArgoCD + TeraSky
# Crossplane) pulled in additional undici transitives:
#   - CVE-2026-109383: Certificate validation bypass via dropped options
#   - CVE-2026-109829: Cache poisoning + information disclosure
#   - CVE-2026-87018:  DoS via TLS renegotiation with malformed cert
# Fix: undici 6.29.1 / 7.30.1 / 8.12.2 (currently on 5.29.0, 7.30.0, 8.11.2
# across transitives). Mitigation: same as earlier undici blocks —
# internal in-cluster HTTP client, not reached by untrusted input;
# cert-validation bypass only applies to Backstage calling OUT to our
# own services (K8s API, GitHub via App) which are known-good.
# Phase 8 security sweep will bump transitives via yarn resolutions.
CVE-2026-109383
CVE-2026-109829
CVE-2026-87018
